SK: I think they were too old. I don't know. Maybe she didn't want any. I don't know. I don't know. She had-- she had a sister that she was close to. And she had nieces. I think she had a brother too, but I don't remember exactly.

INT: OK, let's take a break.

SK: Good idea. Yeah, maybe you should just say something to me, make sure I'm hearing you right.

INT: So we were talking about the Bronx.

SK: OK.

INT: You went to school there.

SK: Right. I went to elementary school there.

INT: And can you describe your life in this new environment?

