INT: What was his name?

SK: My husband? His name was Joel Kane.

INT: Can you please spell it?

SK: His real name was Irving Joel Kane, But they never used the name Irving. Irving was somebody who had passed away in the family. So that was his-- his real, you know, his legal name. So when he signed legal papers, he signed them, Irving Joel Kane. But in the telephone book, he was listed as I. Joel Cain, you know, just the initial I. But anyway, his name is J-O-E-L.

